2:54:11 AM [express] GET /api/reports 304 in 11ms :: [{"id":17,"userId":"53748919","title":"test","rawDescription":"I am reporting a cyber crime incident related to my Instagram account.\n\nOn 5 February 2026, I was unable to log in to my Instagram account @urban.vibes_07. When I tried to reset the password, I noticed that the registered email ID and phone number linked to the account had been changed without my permission.\n\nAfter this, my friends informed me that they received suspicious messages from my account asking for money and sharing unknown links. Some inappropriate content was also posted from my account which I did not upload.\n\nI believe my account was hacked after I clicked on a fake verification link received through a direct message claiming my account would be suspended.\n\nI have already reported this issue to Instagram support and secured my email account. I am requesting verification of this incident and guidance on further actions.","incidentType":"PHISHING","structuredReport":{"impact":"Unauthorized access and control of Instagram account @urban.vibes_07, change of linked email ID and phone number, impersonation through the account, sending of fraudulent money requests and suspicious links to friends, and posting of inappropriate content from the compromised account. Potential reputational damage and possible financial risk to contacts.","guidance":{"evidence":["Take screenshots of the phishing email or SMS, including the sender's details.","Do not delete the original message; it contains technical headers needed for investigation.","Note down the URL of the malicious website if you clicked a link."],"security":["Change passwords for your email and any affected online accounts immediately.","Enable Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) on all sensitive accounts.","Run a full antivirus scan on your device to check for installed malware."],"immediate":["Disconnect your device from the internet to stop further data transmission.","Close all browser tabs and do not interact with the suspicious link or sender.","If you provided bank details, call your bank immediately to freeze your accounts."],"nextSteps":["Report the incident to the official National Cyber Crime Reporting Portal (cybercrime.gov.in).","Notify the organization being impersonated (e.g., your bank or service provider).","Monitor your financial statements for any unauthorized transactions for the next 30 days."]},"nextSteps":["Preserve all available evidence: keep screenshots of the fake verification message, suspicious messages sent from your account, inappropriate posts, email or SMS alerts about changes to your Instagram account, and any communication with Instagram support.","Immediately inform all friends and contacts who may have received messages from your account that it was compromised, advising them not to click any links or send any money related to those messages.","Continue working with Instagram support: follow their account recovery procedure, submit identity verification if requested, and request restoration of original email/phone details and removal of unauthorized posts.","Enable strong security practices on all linked accounts: use unique, strong passwords; enable two-factor authentication (2FA) on Instagram, email, and other social media; and review active sessions/devices to log out unknown devices.","Monitor bank accounts, UPI apps, and digital wallets for any suspicious transactions, especially if any financial details are stored in messages or linked services.","File a formal cyber crime complaint: submit this FIR-style summary along with evidence at your local Cyber Crime Police Station or through the national cyber crime reporting portal (if available in your country).","Request your friends who received money requests or suspicious links to save and share screenshots and message headers, and to provide written statements if required by the investigating officer.","Regularly review your email account security: check account recovery options, recent login activity, and revoke access for unknown third-party apps or services linked to your email or Instagram.","Avoid clicking on verification or security links received via direct messages or unofficial channels in the future; always verify such notices through the official app or website directly.","Stay in contact with the investigating officer and promptly provide any new information or additional evidence that may arise during the course of the investigation."],"description":"To, The Officer-in-Charge, Cyber Crime Police Station.\n\nSubject: Complaint regarding Account Hacking and Misuse of Social Media Account.\n\nI, Information not available at the time of reporting, wish to report a fraudulent incident involving unauthorized access and misuse of my Instagram account.\n\n1. Incident Details\n- Date & Time: On 5 February 2026, exact time not known.\n- Mode of Communication: Instagram direct message containing a fake verification link.\n- Suspect Details: Identity of the person(s) who hacked the account is not known at the time of reporting. The act appears to have been carried out by unknown cyber criminals using a phishing/verification scam.\n\n2. Chronological Description of the Incident\nOn 5 February 2026, I discovered that I was unable to log in to my Instagram account with the username @urban.vibes_07. When I attempted to reset the password, I noticed that the registered email ID and phone number linked to the account had been changed without my knowledge or consent. Prior to this incident, I had clicked on a link received via Instagram direct message that falsely claimed to be an official verification link and stated that my account would be suspended if I did not act. After the account takeover, my friends informed me that they received suspicious messages from my account asking for money and sharing unknown links. Additionally, inappropriate content was posted from my account which I did not upload. These actions were carried out without my authorization and constitute unauthorized access, impersonation, and misuse of my social media identity. I have reported the issue to Instagram support and have taken steps to secure my associated email account.\n\n3. Financial Loss Details (if any)\nAs of the time of reporting, I have not directly incurred any confirmed financial loss. However, my friends and contacts were asked for money through my compromised account, which may have caused or may cause financial loss to them. The exact financial impact, if any, is not known at this stage.\n\n4. Evidence List\n- Screenshots or records of the fake verification message and link received on Instagram (if available).\n- Screenshots of failed login attempts to the Instagram account @urban.vibes_07.\n- Screenshots showing that the registered email ID and phone number on the Instagram account were changed without authorization (if available from notifications or emails).\n- Messages or statements from friends who received suspicious money requests and unknown links from my compromised account.\n- Screenshots or links to inappropriate content posted from the account which I did not upload.\n- Copies of communication and complaint submitted to Instagram support regarding the account hacking.\n\n5. Request for Action\nI respectfully request the Cyber Crime Police Station to:\n- Register my complaint regarding hacking and unauthorized access of my Instagram account @urban.vibes_07.\n- Conduct an investigation to identify the person(s) responsible for the hacking, phishing attempt, and misuse of my account.\n- Coordinate with Instagram/Meta to obtain relevant logs, IP addresses, and account recovery assistance, and to prevent further misuse of the compromised account.\n- Take necessary legal action under the applicable cyber crime and IT laws against the offenders.\n- Provide guidance on any additional steps I should take to protect my online accounts and to safeguard my contacts from further fraud attempts.\n\nI am willing to provide any further information, documents, or evidence required in the investigation.\n\nSincerely,\nInformation not available at the time of reporting.","incidentType":"account_hacking","modeOfAttack":"Instagram direct message with phishing/verification link","extractedDetails":{"date":"5 February 2026","platform":"Instagram","financial_loss":"No direct financial loss reported by complainant; possible financial risk to friends who received money requests","suspect_details":"Unknown cyber criminal(s); no specific identity provided","account_username":"@urban.vibes_07","email_account_status":"Email account secured by the complainant","mode_of_communication":"Instagram direct message","reported_to_platform_support":"Yes, issue reported to Instagram support"},"suggestedCategory":"Cyber-enabled crime involving social media account hacking and phishing-based compromise"},"status":"draft","createdAt":"2026-01-28T14:46:02.488Z"},{"id":16,"userId":"53748919","title":"test","rawDescription":"I am reporting a cyber crime incident related to my Instagram account.\n\nOn 5 February 2026, I was unable to log in to my Instagram account @urban.vibes_07. When I tried to reset the password, I noticed that the registered email ID and phone number linked to the account had been changed without my permission.\n\nAfter this, my friends informed me that they received suspicious messages from my account asking for money and sharing unknown links. Some inappropriate content was also posted from my account which I did not upload.\n\nI believe my account was hacked after I clicked on a fake verification link received through a direct message claiming my account would be suspended.\n\nI have already reported this issue to Instagram support and secured my email account. I am requesting verification of this incident and guidance on further actions.","incidentType":"PHISHING","structuredReport":{"impact":"Unauthorized access and control of Instagram account @urban.vibes_07, change of linked email ID and phone number, misuse of account to send fraudulent messages requesting money and unknown links to friends, posting of inappropriate content, reputational damage, and potential risk of financial loss to contacts.","guidance":{"evidence":["Take screenshots of the phishing email or SMS, including the sender's details.","Do not delete the original message; it contains technical headers needed for investigation.","Note down the URL of the malicious website if you clicked a link."],"security":["Change passwords for your email and any affected online accounts immediately.","Enable Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) on all sensitive accounts.","Run a full antivirus scan on your device to check for installed malware."],"immediate":["Disconnect your device from the internet to stop further data transmission.","Close all browser tabs and do not interact with the suspicious link or sender.","If you provided bank details, call your bank immediately to freeze your accounts."],"nextSteps":["Report the incident to the official National Cyber Crime Reporting Portal (cybercrime.gov.in).","Notify the organization being impersonated (e.g., your bank or service provider).","Monitor your financial statements for any unauthorized transactions for the next 30 days."]},"nextSteps":["Preserve all digital evidence: keep screenshots of the fake verification message, suspicious DMs, inappropriate posts, and any email or SMS alerts from Instagram. Do not delete these.","Collect details from friends who received messages: request them to share screenshots of the messages asking for money or links, along with dates and times if possible.","Obtain and note reference numbers from Instagram: keep any complaint or ticket ID provided by Instagram support, along with the date and mode of your complaint.","Attempt account recovery using official channels: continue using Instagram’s official help pages (Account Compromised and Hacked Account forms) and ensure you only access them via the official app or website.","Run full security checks on other accounts: change passwords on your email and any other accounts that use the same or similar password; enable two-factor authentication (2FA) wherever possible.","Inform your contacts: publicly inform your followers and friends (via other channels) that your Instagram was compromised and that any requests for money or suspicious links from that account should be ignored.","File a formal cyber crime complaint: submit this FIR-style summary, along with evidence, to your local Cyber Crime Police Station or the national cyber crime reporting portal applicable in your country.","Monitor bank and payment accounts: even though no loss is reported yet, regularly review statements for any unusual or unauthorized transactions.","Record a timeline: write down the sequence of events (when you received the verification DM, when you clicked the link, when you lost access, when friends reported suspicious activity) to assist investigators.","Cooperate with law enforcement: be prepared to provide device details (phone/computer used), email IDs, recovery numbers, and any further information the investigating officer may request."],"description":"To,\nThe Officer-in-Charge,\nCyber Crime Police Station.\n\nSubject: Complaint regarding unauthorized access and misuse of Instagram account (account hacking and phishing).\n\nI, Information not available at the time of reporting, wish to report a fraudulent incident involving unauthorized access to and misuse of my Instagram account.\n\n1. Incident Details\n   - Date & Time of Incident: On or around 5 February 2026 (exact time not known).\n   - Mode of Communication: Instagram direct message containing a fake verification link.\n   - Platform/Service Involved: Instagram account with username @urban.vibes_07.\n   - Suspect Details: The identity of the person(s) who gained unauthorized access to my account is not known at the time of reporting.\n\n2. Chronological Description of the Incident\n   On 5 February 2026, I discovered that I was unable to log in to my Instagram account @urban.vibes_07. When I attempted to reset the password using the usual recovery options, I observed that the registered email ID and phone number linked to the account had been changed without my knowledge or consent.\n\n   Prior to this incident, I had received a message through Instagram direct message which appeared to be an official verification or suspension notice, stating that my account would be suspended unless I completed a verification process. The message contained a link which I clicked, believing it to be legitimate. I believe that this link was fraudulent and used to compromise my account credentials.\n\n   After the unauthorized access occurred, several of my friends informed me that they had received suspicious messages from my Instagram account, including requests for money and unknown links. Additionally, inappropriate content was posted from my account which I did not upload or authorize. These actions have harmed my online reputation and may have exposed my contacts to further fraud attempts.\n\n   I have since reported the issue to Instagram support and taken steps to secure my associated email account. However, my Instagram account remains compromised or under risk, and the extent of misuse of my personal data is not fully known.\n\n3. Financial Loss Details (if any)\n   At the time of reporting, I am not aware of any direct financial loss to myself. However, my friends and contacts may have been requested to send money, and there is a potential risk of financial fraud against them. Exact amounts and victim details are not available at the time of reporting.\n\n4. Evidence List\n   - Screenshots or records of the Instagram direct message containing the fake verification link (if available).\n   - Screenshots showing inability to log in and any error messages from Instagram.\n   - Screenshots showing that the registered email ID and phone number on the Instagram account have been changed.\n   - Screenshots or copies of suspicious messages sent from my compromised account to my friends requesting money or sharing unknown links (if shared by them).\n   - Screenshots of inappropriate posts made from the compromised account which I did not upload.\n   - Copies of communication and complaint reference numbers submitted to Instagram support.\n   - Any email alerts from Instagram regarding login from new devices, password changes, or changes to account recovery information (if available).\n\n5. Request for Action\n   I respectfully request the Cyber Crime Police Station to:\n   - Register this complaint as a cyber crime incident involving account hacking and phishing.\n   - Conduct an investigation to identify the person(s) who gained unauthorized access to my Instagram account and misused it to send fraudulent messages and post inappropriate content.\n   - Coordinate with Instagram/Meta to secure and restore my account, reverse unauthorized changes to the registered email and phone number, and obtain necessary logs and technical data (such as IP addresses, device details, and timestamps) associated with the unauthorized access.\n   - Take appropriate legal action against the offenders under applicable cyber crime and IT laws.\n   - Provide guidance on any further steps I should take to protect my personal data, prevent further misuse, and inform my contacts about the potential risk.\n\n   I am willing to cooperate fully with the investigation and provide any additional information or documents required.\n\nYours faithfully,\nInformation not available at the time of reporting.","incidentType":"account_hacking","modeOfAttack":"Instagram direct message containing a phishing/verification link","extractedDetails":{"date":"5 February 2026","platform":"Instagram","financial_loss":"No direct financial loss reported by complainant at the time of reporting","suspect_details":"Not known","account_username":"@urban.vibes_07","nature_of_misuse":"Requests for money sent to friends, unknown links shared, and inappropriate content posted from the account","email_account_status":"Secured by complainant after the incident","reported_to_platform":"Instagram support","mode_of_communication":"Instagram direct message"},"suggestedCategory":"Cyber-enabled fraud and social media account compromise (account hacking and phishing)"},"status":"draft","createdAt":"2026-01-28T14:46:00.108Z"},{"id":15,"userId":"53748919","title":"xyz","rawDescription":"I am reporting a cyber crime incident related to my Instagram account.\n\nOn 5 February 2026, I was unable to log in to my Instagram account @urban.vibes_07. When I tried to reset the password, I noticed that the registered email ID and phone number linked to the account had been changed without my permission.\n\nAfter this, my friends informed me that they received suspicious messages from my account asking for money and sharing unknown links. Some inappropriate content was also posted from my account which I did not upload.\n\nI believe my account was hacked after I clicked on a fake verification link received through a direct message claiming my account would be suspended.\n\nI have already reported this issue to Instagram support and secured my email account. I am requesting verification of this incident and guidance on further actions.","incidentType":"PHISHING","structuredReport":{"impact":"Unauthorized access to Instagram account @urban.vibes_07, change of registered email ID and phone number, loss of control over the account, impersonation of the complainant, sending of fraudulent messages requesting money to friends, sharing of unknown/malicious links, posting of inappropriate content damaging reputation, and potential financial loss to friends or contacts.","guidance":{"evidence":["Take screenshots of the phishing email or SMS, including the sender's details.","Do not delete the original message; it contains technical headers needed for investigation.","Note down the URL of the malicious website if you clicked a link."],"security":["Change passwords for your email and any affected online accounts immediately.","Enable Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) on all sensitive accounts.","Run a full antivirus scan on your device to check for installed malware."],"immediate":["Disconnect your device from the internet to stop further data transmission.","Close all browser tabs and do not interact with the suspicious link or sender.","If you provided bank details, call your bank immediately to freeze your accounts."],"nextSteps":["Report the incident to the official National Cyber Crime Reporting Portal (cybercrime.gov.in).","Notify the organization being impersonated (e.g., your bank or service provider).","Monitor your financial statements for any unauthorized transactions for the next 30 days."]},"nextSteps":["Preserve all available evidence: save and screenshot the fake verification message, any suspicious messages sent from your account, and any inappropriate posts. Do not delete these, as they may be needed for investigation.","Collect written statements or screenshots from friends who received suspicious messages or links from your account, including dates, times, and the exact content of the messages.","Retain all emails or in-app notifications from Instagram relating to login attempts, security alerts, or your existing complaint ticket/acknowledgment.","Immediately enable strong security measures on all related accounts (email, other social media, and phone accounts): update passwords to unique, strong passwords and enable two‑factor authentication wherever possible.","Continue following up with Instagram support using your existing case or ticket number, requesting (a) restoration of access, (b) reversal of unauthorized email/phone changes, and (c) temporary suspension of the account if misuse is ongoing.","File an official cyber crime complaint through your national/state cyber crime reporting portal or by visiting the nearest Cyber Crime Police Station, enclosing all screenshots, correspondence with Instagram, and a copy of this structured statement.","Inform your friends and contacts via alternative channels that your Instagram account was compromised, cautioning them not to send money or click on links received from your account during the incident period.","Monitor bank accounts, e‑wallets, and other financial apps for any unusual activity; if any fraudulent transactions are noticed, immediately inform the respective bank or payment service and lodge a separate financial fraud complaint.","Regularly check whether any other online accounts show signs of unauthorized access, and if so, change credentials and log out of all active sessions.","Keep a dated record of all steps you have taken (reports to Instagram, emails, police/portal complaint numbers) so you can provide a clear timeline to investigating authorities."],"description":"To, The Officer-in-Charge, Cyber Crime Police Station.\n\nSubject: Complaint regarding account_hacking and phishing incident on Instagram.\n\nI, Information not available at the time of reporting, wish to report a fraudulent incident involving unauthorized access and misuse of my Instagram social media account.\n\n1. Incident Details\n   - Date & Time: On 5 February 2026; exact time is information not available at the time of reporting.\n   - Mode of Communication: Instagram direct message containing a fake verification link.\n   - Platform Involved: Instagram account with username @urban.vibes_07.\n   - Suspect Details: Unknown persons; no specific identity or contact details are known at the time of reporting.\n\n2. Chronological Description of the Incident\n   On 5 February 2026, I was unable to log in to my Instagram account with username @urban.vibes_07. When I attempted to reset the password, I observed that the registered email ID and phone number associated with the account had been changed without my knowledge or consent. Prior to losing access, I had clicked on a link received through an Instagram direct message claiming to be an account verification notice and warning that my account would be suspended if I did not act. I now believe this link was fraudulent and used to compromise my account.\n\n   After the compromise, my friends and contacts informed me that they received suspicious messages from my Instagram account asking for money and sharing unknown and potentially malicious links. Additionally, inappropriate content was posted from my account which I did not upload or authorize. This clearly indicates that an unknown cyber criminal gained unauthorized control over my account and misused it to conduct fraudulent and possibly harmful activities using my identity and social media presence.\n\n   I have reported the incident to Instagram support and initiated steps to secure my linked email account. However, the account remains compromised or uncertain, and the misuse of my identity and reputation continues to be a serious concern.\n\n3. Financial Loss Details (if any)\n   As of the time of reporting, I have not suffered a confirmed direct financial loss. However, there is a risk that my friends or contacts may have suffered financial loss if they transferred money based on the fraudulent messages sent from my account. The exact financial impact is information not available at the time of reporting.\n\n4. Evidence List\n   - Screenshots (or potential screenshots) of the login failure and account recovery attempts indicating that the email ID and phone number were changed without authorization.\n   - Screenshots or copies of the fraudulent Instagram direct message containing the fake verification link claiming account suspension.\n   - Screenshots of suspicious messages sent from my account to friends requesting money and sharing unknown links (as provided by friends or contacts).\n   - Screenshots or records of inappropriate posts made from my Instagram account which I did not upload.\n   - Confirmation or acknowledgment emails from Instagram support regarding the complaint already submitted.\n   - Any email security alerts related to my linked email account which I have since secured.\n\n5. Request for Action\n   I respectfully request the Cyber Crime Police Station to:\n   (a) Register my complaint regarding the hacking and misuse of my Instagram account @urban.vibes_07.\n   (b) Coordinate with Instagram and relevant service providers to secure and restore my account access, and to obtain logs, IP addresses, and technical details related to the unauthorized access and changes to the account.\n   (c) Investigate and identify the unknown persons involved in sending fraudulent messages and posting inappropriate content from my account.\n   (d) Take appropriate legal action against the offenders under applicable cyber crime and information technology laws.\n   (e) Advise me on further steps to protect my other online accounts and prevent additional misuse of my identity.\n\nI affirm that the information provided in this complaint is true and correct to the best of my knowledge and belief at the time of reporting.","incidentType":"account_hacking","modeOfAttack":"Instagram direct message with a phishing/verification link","extractedDetails":{"date":"5 February 2026","platform":"Instagram","loss_amount":"Information not available at the time of reporting","probable_cause":"Clicked on a fake verification link received via Instagram direct message claiming account suspension risk","account_changes":"Registered email ID and phone number linked to the account were changed without permission","observed_misuse":["Suspicious messages from the account asking for money","Messages sharing unknown links","Inappropriate content posted from the account"],"suspect_details":"Unknown persons; no identifiable details provided","account_username":"@urban.vibes_07","email_account_status":"Secured after the incident","reported_to_platform":"Instagram support","mode_of_communication":"Instagram direct message"},"suggestedCategory":"Social media account takeover and phishing-based cyber fraud"},"status":"draft","createdAt":"2026-01-28T14:41:18.311Z"},{"id":14,"userId":"53748919","title":"suspicious","rawDescription":"I am reporting a cyber crime incident related to my Instagram account.\n\nOn 5 February 2026, I was unable to log in to my Instagram account @urban.vibes_07. When I tried to reset the password, I noticed that the registered email ID and phone number linked to the account had been changed without my permission.\n\nAfter this, my friends informed me that they received suspicious messages from my account asking for money and sharing unknown links. Some inappropriate content was also posted from my account which I did not upload.\n\nI believe my account was hacked after I clicked on a fake verification link received through a direct message claiming my account would be suspended.\n\nI have already reported this issue to Instagram support and secured my email account. I am requesting verification of this incident and guidance on further actions.","incidentType":"Social media account compromise / phishing-related cybercrime","structuredReport":{"platform":"Instagram","timeline":[{"date":"2026-02-05","event":"User was unable to log in to Instagram account @urban.vibes_07."},{"date":"2026-02-05","event":"During password reset attempt, user discovered that the registered email address and phone number for the account had been changed without permission."},{"date":"2026-02-05","event":"Friends of the user reported receiving suspicious messages from the compromised account asking for money and sharing unknown links."},{"date":"2026-02-05","event":"Inappropriate content was posted from the Instagram account without the owner’s knowledge or consent."},{"date":"2026-02-05","event":"User identified a likely cause: previously clicked on a fake verification link received via Instagram direct message, claiming the account would be suspended, which is suspected to have led to the compromise."},{"date":"2026-02-05","event":"User reported the incident to Instagram support and secured their associated email account."}],"reportedBy":"Owner of Instagram account @urban.vibes_07","threatType":["Account takeover","Phishing","Impersonation/fraud"],"description":"The Instagram account @urban.vibes_07 was compromised on or before 5 February 2026. The account owner was suddenly unable to log in and, during password reset attempts, observed that the registered email address and phone number linked to the account had been changed without authorization. After the unauthorized access began, the attacker used the compromised account to send fraudulent messages to the victim’s contacts, asking for money and sharing suspicious/unknown links. Inappropriate content was also posted from the account without the owner’s consent. The victim believes the compromise occurred after clicking on a fake Instagram verification link received via direct message, which falsely claimed the account would be suspended unless verified. This indicates a phishing-based credential theft leading to account takeover.","attackVector":"Phishing link (fake Instagram verification link) delivered via Instagram direct message","incidentDate":"2026-02-05","incidentType":"Social media account compromise / phishing-related cybercrime","accountHandle":"@urban.vibes_07","impactedAssets":["Instagram account @urban.vibes_07","Reputation and trust with contacts/friends on Instagram"],"suspectedCause":"User clicked on a fraudulent verification link that likely captured login credentials and enabled unauthorized access to the Instagram account.","detectionMethod":"User noticed inability to log in and observed unauthorized changes to account recovery details","actionsAlreadyTaken":["Reported the compromised account and incident to Instagram support","Secured the associated email account (e.g., changed password, likely enabled security measures)"],"requestedAssistance":["Verification/official acknowledgment of the cyber incident","Guidance on additional steps to recover and secure the Instagram account","Advice on preventing further misuse and protecting against similar attacks"],"recommendedNextSteps":["Continue following up with Instagram support using their official help center and account recovery forms to regain control of the account.","Provide Instagram with proof of identity and any supporting evidence (screenshots, messages from friends, timestamps) to strengthen the recovery request.","Enable multi-factor authentication (2FA) on Instagram and all linked accounts (email, phone, other social platforms) once access is regained.","Inform friends and contacts that the account was compromised, advise them to ignore and delete suspicious messages and links sent previously, and to report the account if they see ongoing suspicious activity.","Review all devices and sessions associated with email and social accounts, revoke unknown sessions, and update passwords with strong, unique combinations.","Report the phishing attempt and account compromise to local cybercrime authorities or a cybercrime reporting portal, if available in the relevant jurisdiction."],"indicatorsOfCompromise":["Sudden inability to log in to Instagram account","Unauthorized change of registered email address on the Instagram account","Unauthorized change of registered phone number on the Instagram account","Friends receiving messages from the account requesting money","Friends receiving suspicious/unknown links from the account","Inappropriate content posted from the account without owner’s consent"]},"status":"draft","createdAt":"2026-01-28T14:38:09.968Z"},{"id":13,"userId":"53748919","title":"akshaya","rawDescription":"I am reporting a cyber crime incident related to my Instagram account.\n\nOn 5 February 2026, I was unable to log in to my Instagram account @urban.vibes_07. When I tried to reset the password, I noticed that the registered email ID and phone number linked to the account had been changed without my permission.\n\nAfter this, my friends informed me that they received suspicious messages from my account asking for money and sharing unknown links. Some inappropriate content was also posted from my account which I did not upload.\n\nI believe my account was hacked after I clicked on a fake verification link received through a direct message claiming my account would be suspended.\n\nI have already reported this issue to Instagram support and secured my email account. I am requesting verification of this incident and guidance on further actions.","incidentType":"Social media account compromise / phishing-based account takeover","structuredReport":{"summary":"The victim’s Instagram account was compromised after interacting with a phishing link posing as an account verification/suspension notice. The attacker changed the recovery email and phone number, sent fraudulent messages to contacts, and posted unauthorized content.","platform":"Instagram","reportDate":"2026-02-05","attackVector":{"type":"Phishing","description":"A fraudulent Instagram ‘verification / account suspension’ link sent via direct message was used to trick the victim into revealing account credentials or session information, enabling unauthorized access."},"incidentType":"Social media account compromise / phishing-based account takeover","reporterRole":"Account owner","accountHandle":"@urban.vibes_07","dateOfIncident":"2026-02-05","impactedAssets":["Instagram account @urban.vibes_07 (credentials, profile control)","Contacts/followers receiving scam messages and links","Reputation of the account owner due to inappropriate posts"],"riskAssessment":{"primaryRisks":["Ongoing impersonation and fraud targeting contacts","Reputational damage due to inappropriate content","Potential credential reuse attacks against other services if passwords are reused"],"likelihoodOfOngoingRisk":"Medium to High (attacker currently controls account and may continue scams/impersonation until access is revoked)."},"timelineOfEvents":[{"date":"2026-02-05","event":"Victim unable to log into Instagram account @urban.vibes_07."},{"date":"2026-02-05","event":"Victim attempts password reset and notices that the registered email address and phone number linked to the account have been changed without permission."},{"date":"2026-02-05","event":"Friends report receiving suspicious messages from the victim’s account asking for money and sharing unknown links; inappropriate content is also posted from the account."},{"date":"2026-02-05","event":"Victim recalls clicking on a fake Instagram verification/suspension link received via direct message, suspected as the initial compromise vector."},{"date":"2026-02-05","event":"Victim reports the incident to Instagram support and secures the associated email account."}],"evidenceMentioned":["Failed login attempts to the original account","Changed email ID and phone number visible during password reset process","Reports from friends confirming suspicious money-asking messages and unknown links","Inappropriate posts visible on the compromised account","Prior receipt of a fake verification / suspension link via direct message"],"jurisdictionNotes":"The user did not specify country or region; exact procedures and reporting channels may vary depending on local cybercrime laws and available authorities.","actionsAlreadyTaken":["Reported the issue to Instagram support","Secured the associated email account"],"requestedAssistance":["Verification/official acknowledgement that the account was compromised","Guidance on further actions to secure the account and mitigate damage"],"suspectedThreatType":["Account takeover","Social engineering / phishing fraud","Impersonation and fraud (attempted financial scams using the victim’s identity)"],"recommendedNextSteps":["Continue working with Instagram account recovery process (using identity verification, past device/IP logs, or prior email/phone details where possible).","Inform friends and followers that the account has been compromised and warn them not to interact with any suspicious messages/links or send money.","Review and secure all other accounts using the same email or similar passwords (enable strong, unique passwords and two-factor authentication wherever possible).","Preserve evidence (screenshots of suspicious messages, changed account details, and phishing link) for any formal cybercrime or law-enforcement report.","File a cybercrime complaint with local law enforcement or national cybercrime portal, referencing the phishing link and account takeover, if available in the jurisdiction.","Run malware/virus scans on devices used to access Instagram, especially the device on which the phishing link was opened, to rule out additional compromise."],"observedMaliciousActivity":["Unauthorized change of registered email ID and phone number on the Instagram account","Unauthorized login and control of the Instagram account","Sending fraudulent messages from the compromised account requesting money","Sending unknown/suspicious links to contacts","Posting inappropriate content not uploaded by the victim"]},"status":"draft","createdAt":"2026-01-28T14:34:37.818Z"},{"id":12,"userId":"53748919","title":"akshaya","rawDescription":"I am reporting a cyber crime incident related to my Instagram account.\n\nOn 5 February 2026, I was unable to log in to my Instagram account @urban.vibes_07. When I tried to reset the password, I noticed that the registered email ID and phone number linked to the account had been changed without my permission.\n\nAfter this, my friends informed me that they received suspicious messages from my account asking for money and sharing unknown links. Some inappropriate content was also posted from my account which I did not upload.\n\nI believe my account was hacked after I clicked on a fake verification link received through a direct message claiming my account would be suspended.\n\nI have already reported this issue to Instagram support and secured my email account. I am requesting verification of this incident and guidance on further actions.","incidentType":"Social media account compromise / cyber fraud","structuredReport":{"impact":{"lossOfAccess":true,"dataExposureRisk":"Possible exposure of personal information associated with the Instagram account","reputationalRisk":"Contacts received scam messages and inappropriate posts appeared under user’s name","accountLockoutDetails":"User unable to log in to Instagram account due to changed email and phone number","potentialFinancialRisk":"Friends were solicited for money from the compromised account"},"summary":"On 5 February 2026, the reporter’s Instagram account @urban.vibes_07 was likely compromised after they clicked a fake verification link received via direct message. Following the compromise, the attacker changed the registered email and phone number, locked the reporter out, sent fraudulent money‑request messages and unknown links to the reporter’s contacts, and posted inappropriate content. The reporter has notified Instagram support and secured their email account, and now seeks formal recognition of the incident as a cyber crime and guidance on further remedial actions.","platform":"Instagram","isOngoing":true,"reportDate":"2026-02-05","incidentType":"Social media account compromise / cyber fraud","accountHandle":"urban.vibes_07","modusOperandi":{"attackVector":"Phishing link received via Instagram direct message","probableCompromiseCause":"User clicked on fake verification link, likely revealing login credentials to attacker","phishingContentDescription":"Message claiming the account would be suspended and asking the user to click a verification link","subsequentActionsByAttacker":["Changed the email ID linked to the Instagram account","Changed the phone number linked to the Instagram account","Sent messages to friends/contacts asking for money","Shared unknown/suspicious links with contacts","Posted inappropriate content from the compromised account"]},"primaryIssues":["Unauthorized access to Instagram account","Change of registered email and phone number without consent","Impersonation and fraudulent messages sent to contacts","Posting of inappropriate content without authorization","Phishing via fake verification link"],"dateOfIncident":"2026-02-05","confidenceLevel":"high","jurisdictionNotes":"Exact country/jurisdiction is not specified; user should report via the official national cybercrime/online fraud reporting portal or local police cyber cell.","requestedAssistance":["Verification/recognition of the incident as a cyber crime / account hacking","Guidance on further steps to recover the account and prevent further misuse"],"reporterActionsTaken":["Attempted password reset on Instagram","Identified that registered email and phone number were changed","Reported the incident to Instagram support","Secured associated email account (e.g., changed password, likely enabled security measures)"],"recommendedNextStepsForReporter":["Continue coordinating with Instagram support to regain account access (submit identity verification and recovery forms as requested)","Enable two‑factor authentication (2FA) on Instagram and all linked email/phone accounts once access is restored","Notify friends and contacts that the account was compromised and warn them not to click any links or send money","Preserve evidence: take screenshots of fraudulent messages, posts, and any communication with Instagram support","Run malware/antivirus scans on devices used to access the phishing link","Change passwords for other online accounts that use similar credentials","File a formal cyber crime complaint with local law enforcement or national cybercrime portal, attaching all evidence"]},"status":"draft","createdAt":"2026-01-28T14:34:35.646Z"},{"id":11,"userId":"53748919","title":"akshaya","rawDescription":"I am reporting a cyber crime incident related to my Instagram account.\n\nOn 5 February 2026, I was unable to log in to my Instagram account @urban.vibes_07. When I tried to reset the password, I noticed that the registered email ID and phone number linked to the account had been changed without my permission.\n\nAfter this, my friends informed me that they received suspicious messages from my account asking for money and sharing unknown links. Some inappropriate content was also posted from my account which I did not upload.\n\nI believe my account was hacked after I clicked on a fake verification link received through a direct message claiming my account would be suspended.\n\nI have already reported this issue to Instagram support and secured my email account. I am requesting verification of this incident and guidance on further actions.","incidentType":"Social Media Account Compromise","structuredReport":{"victim":{"role":"Individual user","username":"@urban.vibes_07","contactChangedWithoutConsent":true},"summary":"The reporting party's Instagram account was compromised, contact details were changed without authorization, and the account was used to send fraudulent messages and post inappropriate content after the victim clicked a fake verification link.","platform":"Instagram","reportDate":"2026-02-05","description":"On 5 February 2026, the reporting individual was unable to log in to their Instagram account @urban.vibes_07. When attempting to reset the password, they discovered that the registered email address and phone number associated with the account had been changed without their consent. Following this, friends of the reporting individual received suspicious messages from the compromised Instagram account requesting money and sharing unknown links. Additionally, inappropriate content was posted from the account that the reporting individual did not upload. The individual believes the account was hacked after they clicked on a fraudulent verification link received via Instagram direct message, which falsely claimed that their account would be suspended. The incident has been reported to Instagram support, and the individual has secured their email account. They are seeking official verification of the incident and guidance on any further steps to take.","attackVector":"Phishing via Instagram direct message containing a fake verification/suspension link","incidentType":"Social Media Account Compromise","accountHandle":"@urban.vibes_07","threatActions":["Unauthorized access to social media account","Modification of account recovery details (email and phone number)","Impersonation of the victim to contacts","Social engineering to solicit money from contacts","Distribution of potentially malicious links","Posting of unauthorized/inappropriate content"],"dateOfIncident":"2026-02-05","suspectedCause":"Account credentials harvested through a phishing link posing as an official Instagram verification/suspension notice.","severityAssessment":{"integrityImpact":"High – attacker altered recovery details and posted/communicated content as the victim.","overallSeverity":"High","availabilityImpact":"High – victim has lost access to the Instagram account.","confidentialityImpact":"Medium – unauthorized access to social media account and contact list; potential exposure of private messages depending on attacker actions."},"actionsAlreadyTaken":["Reported the incident to Instagram support","Secured the associated email account"],"requestedAssistance":["Verification/acknowledgment of the cyber crime incident","Guidance on additional protective and remedial steps (e.g., further account recovery, evidence preservation, protection of contacts)"],"dataOrAssetsAffected":["Instagram account @urban.vibes_07","Account recovery information (email and phone number associated with the Instagram account)","Contacts/followers who received fraudulent messages and links"],"recommendedNextSteps":{"technical":["Continue working with Instagram support to regain control of the account and revert unauthorized changes to email and phone number.","Enable two-factor authentication (2FA) on Instagram and all linked accounts once access is restored.","Change passwords for any other accounts that use the same or similar credentials.","Review and revoke access for any unknown third-party apps connected to Instagram."],"notification":["Inform friends and followers that the account was compromised and warn them not to engage with prior suspicious messages or links.","Advise any contacts who interacted with the malicious links to scan their devices for malware and change their passwords."],"legalOrOfficial":["File a formal cyber crime report with local law enforcement or the national cyber crime portal, providing all documented evidence.","Provide a copy of any official report numbers to Instagram if requested to assist with recovery and investigation."],"evidencePreservation":["Keep screenshots or records of suspicious messages sent from the account.","Retain any phishing messages and links received, including the original fake verification DM if possible.","Document dates/times of all notable events and communications with Instagram support."]},"indicatorsOfCompromise":["Inability to log in to Instagram account","Unrecognized change of registered email ID and phone number","Friends receiving suspicious messages requesting money","Friends receiving unknown/malicious links from the account","Inappropriate content posted without the account owner’s knowledge"]},"status":"draft","createdAt":"2026-01-28T14:34:33.552Z"},{"id":10,"userId":"53748919","title":"akshaya","rawDescription":"I am reporting a cyber crime incident related to my Instagram account.\n\nOn 5 February 2026, I was unable to log in to my Instagram account @urban.vibes_07. When I tried to reset the password, I noticed that the registered email ID and phone number linked to the account had been changed without my permission.\n\nAfter this, my friends informed me that they received suspicious messages from my account asking for money and sharing unknown links. Some inappropriate content was also posted from my account which I did not upload.\n\nI believe my account was hacked after I clicked on a fake verification link received through a direct message claiming my account would be suspended.\n\nI have already reported this issue to Instagram support and secured my email account. I am requesting verification of this incident and guidance on further actions.","incidentType":"Social media account compromise","structuredReport":{"summary":"The reporting party’s Instagram account was compromised, with contact details changed, unauthorized messages sent to friends requesting money, suspicious links shared, and inappropriate content posted.","platform":"Instagram","timeline":[{"date":"2026-02-05","event":"User unable to log in to Instagram account @urban.vibes_07."},{"date":"2026-02-05","event":"User attempts password reset and discovers the registered email and phone number have been changed without permission."},{"date":"2026-02-05","event":"Friends report receiving suspicious money-request messages and unknown links from the user’s Instagram account; inappropriate content is posted from the account."},{"date":"2026-02-05","event":"User identifies likely cause as clicking on a fake Instagram verification link received via direct message."},{"date":"2026-02-05","event":"User reports incident to Instagram support and secures associated email account."}],"description":"On 5 February 2026, the reporting party was unable to access their Instagram account (@urban.vibes_07). When attempting to reset the password, they discovered that the account’s registered email ID and phone number had been changed without their authorization. Subsequently, friends reported receiving suspicious messages from the compromised account, including requests for money and unknown links. Inappropriate content was also posted from the account without the owner’s knowledge or consent. The reporting party believes the compromise occurred after clicking on a fraudulent verification link received via Instagram direct message, which claimed the account would be suspended if no action was taken. The user has reported the incident to Instagram support and secured their email account, and they are seeking official verification of the incident and guidance on further actions.","attackVector":"Phishing via direct message with a fake Instagram verification/suspension link","incidentType":"Social media account compromise","accountHandle":"@urban.vibes_07","classification":{"category":"Cyber crime","confidence":"high","subcategory":"Account takeover / phishing"},"dateOfIncident":"2026-02-05","impactedAssets":[{"type":"Social media account","platform":"Instagram","identifier":"@urban.vibes_07"},{"type":"Personal contacts","platform":"Instagram direct messages","description":"Friends/followers who received fraudulent messages and links from the compromised account"}],"suspectedCause":"User clicked on a fake Instagram verification link received via direct message, leading to credential compromise and account takeover.","detectionMethod":"User noticed inability to log in and failed password reset due to changed email and phone number","requestedSupport":["Verification/acknowledgment of the cyber crime incident","Guidance on additional steps to recover and secure the account","Advice on protecting contacts affected by fraudulent messages from the compromised account"],"userActionsTaken":["Attempted password reset on Instagram","Reported the incident to Instagram support","Secured associated email account"],"unauthorizedActivities":["Change of account recovery email","Change of account recovery phone number","Sending fraudulent messages requesting money to contacts","Sending suspicious/unknown links to contacts","Posting inappropriate content from the account"]},"status":"draft","createdAt":"2026-01-28T14:34:28.543Z"},{"id":9,"userId":"53748919","title":"example","rawDescription":"I am reporting a cyber crime incident related to my Instagram account.\n\nOn 5 February 2026, I was unable to log in to my Instagram account @urban.vibes_07. When I tried to reset the password, I noticed that the registered email ID and phone number linked to the account had been changed without my permission.\n\nAfter this, my friends informed me that they received suspicious messages from my account asking for money and sharing unknown links. Some inappropriate content was also posted from my account which I did not upload.\n\nI believe my account was hacked after I clicked on a fake verification link received through a direct message claiming my account would be suspended.\n\nI have already reported this issue to Instagram support and secured my email account. I am requesting verification of this incident and guidance on further actions.","incidentType":"Social media account compromise","structuredReport":{"platform":"Instagram","description":"The user’s Instagram account @urban.vibes_07 appears to have been compromised on 5 February 2026, likely via a phishing link that falsely claimed to be an account verification/suspension notice. After clicking the link, the attacker seems to have taken control of the account, changed the registered email and phone number, and used the account to send fraudulent money requests and suspicious links to the user’s friends, as well as to post inappropriate content. The user has reported the case to Instagram and secured their email, and is seeking confirmation that this is a cybercrime incident and advice on further remediation steps.","incidentType":"Social media account compromise","accountHandle":"@urban.vibes_07","initialVector":"Phishing link received via Instagram direct message claiming account verification / suspension","dateOfIncident":"2026-02-05","detectionMethod":"User was unable to log in and saw that the account’s registered email and phone number had been changed without permission","impactedParties":["Account owner","Friends and contacts who received fraudulent messages/links"],"userActionsTaken":["Attempted password reset on Instagram","Reported the issue to Instagram support","Secured and protected associated email account"],"requestedAssistance":["Verification/official acknowledgment of the cyber incident","Guidance on further actions to secure accounts and mitigate harm"],"recommendedNextSteps":["Preserve evidence: take screenshots of suspicious messages, posts, emails, and any phishing links or DMs received.","Formal complaint: file a cybercrime report with local law enforcement or national cybercrime portal, attaching all evidence, including this incident summary.","Instagram recovery: continue the account recovery process using Instagram’s hacked account procedures, including identity verification if required.","Notify contacts: inform friends and followers that the account was compromised and that any recent money requests or suspicious links should be ignored and reported.","Device and account security: run antivirus/malware scans on devices, change passwords on all major accounts (email, banking, other social media), and enable two-factor authentication wherever possible.","Ongoing monitoring: monitor financial accounts and emails for further suspicious activity or attempted logins."],"unauthorizedActivities":["Change of registered email address and phone number on the Instagram account","Sending fraudulent messages to friends asking for money","Sending suspicious/unknown links to contacts","Posting inappropriate content from the compromised account"]},"status":"draft","createdAt":"2026-01-28T14:23:18.292Z"},{"id":8,"userId":"53748919","title":"Telegram incident","rawDescription":"On 18 March 2026, I came across a job advertisement on a messaging platform claiming to offer a work-from-home data entry job with a high salary. I was contacted by a person using the name “HR Ananya” through a Telegram account named @QuickHire_HR.\n\nThe person informed me that I had been shortlisted for the job and asked me to complete a registration process. As part of this process, I was asked to pay a registration fee of ₹2,500 and a security deposit of ₹3,000, promising that the amount would be refunded after joining.","incidentType":"Online job scam","structuredReport":{"summary":"Victim was approached via Telegram with a fake work-from-home data entry job offer and was asked to pay upfront registration and security fees with a promise of refund after joining.","redFlags":["Unsolicited or informal job approach via messaging platform","Job offer promising high salary for simple work-from-home data entry","Request for upfront registration fee","Request for refundable security deposit","Recruitment being conducted entirely through Telegram","Pressure to pay before any formal employment contract or verification"],"description":"On 18 March 2026, the victim saw a job advertisement on a messaging platform promoting a work-from-home data entry position with a high salary. The victim was then contacted by a person identifying as 'HR Ananya' via a Telegram account with the handle @QuickHire_HR. The individual claimed the victim had been shortlisted for the job and instructed them to complete a registration process. As part of this process, the victim was asked to pay a registration fee of ₹2,500 and a security deposit of ₹3,000, with assurances that these amounts would be refunded after joining. The circumstances indicate a likely fraudulent job recruitment scheme requiring upfront payment.","incidentType":"Online job scam","likelyOutcome":"Attempted financial loss through advance fee payment for a non-existent or fraudulent job opportunity.","victimActions":["Viewed a work-from-home job advertisement on a messaging platform","Engaged in conversation with a Telegram account claiming to be HR","Was instructed to complete a registration process involving upfront payments"],"dateOfIncident":"2026-03-18","amountsRequested":[{"type":"Registration fee","amount":2500,"currency":"INR"},{"type":"Security deposit","amount":3000,"currency":"INR"}],"platformsInvolved":["Messaging platform (unspecified)","Telegram"],"requestedNextSteps":[],"communicationHandles":[{"name":"HR Ananya","handle":"@QuickHire_HR","platform":"Telegram"}],"totalAmountRequested":{"amount":5500,"currency":"INR"},"classificationConfidence":"high"},"status":"draft","createdAt":"2026-01-27T05:30:39.331Z"},{"id":7,"userId":"53748919","title":"Instagram account misuse","rawDescription":"On 5 February 2026, I was unable to log in to my Instagram account named @urban.vibes_07. When I attempted to reset my password, I discovered that the registered email ID and mobile number associated with the account had been changed without my consent.\n\nSoon after, my friends informed me that they were receiving suspicious messages from my Instagram account @urban.vibes_07, requesting money and sharing unknown links. Some messages also contained inappropriate content which I never posted.","incidentType":"Social media account compromise","structuredReport":{"victims":["Account owner of @urban.vibes_07 (loss of access and reputational harm)","Friends and contacts receiving fraudulent and potentially harmful messages"],"platform":"Instagram","description":"On 5 February 2026, the owner of Instagram account @urban.vibes_07 discovered they were unable to log in. During password reset attempts, they found that the registered email ID and mobile number for the account had been changed without their consent, indicating that an unauthorized party had taken control of the account. Shortly afterward, friends reported receiving suspicious messages from @urban.vibes_07 requesting money, sharing unknown links, and containing inappropriate content that the legitimate account owner did not create or send.","incidentType":"Social media account compromise","likelyMethod":"Account credential compromise followed by modification of recovery contact details (email and phone number), enabling the attacker to maintain control and misuse the account for scams and distribution of malicious or inappropriate content.","accountHandle":"@urban.vibes_07","primaryImpacts":["Loss of access to Instagram account","Potential financial fraud targeting friends/contacts","Reputational damage due to inappropriate content sent from the account"],"dateOfDiscovery":"2026-02-05","unauthorizedChanges":["Registered email ID changed without consent","Registered mobile number changed without consent","Account login credentials effectively taken over"],"observedMaliciousActivity":["Suspicious messages sent from the account requesting money","Messages containing unknown or potentially malicious links","Messages with inappropriate content not authored by the legitimate owner"]},"status":"draft","createdAt":"2026-01-27T05:24:36.611Z"},{"id":6,"userId":"53748919","title":"Instagram account misuse","rawDescription":"On 5 February 2026, I was unable to log in to my Instagram account named @urban.vibes_07. When I attempted to reset my password, I discovered that the registered email ID and mobile number associated with the account had been changed without my consent.\n\nSoon after, my friends informed me that they were receiving suspicious messages from my Instagram account @urban.vibes_07, requesting money and sharing unknown links. Some messages also contained inappropriate content which I never posted.","incidentType":"Social media account compromise","structuredReport":{"status":"Ongoing; account owner currently has no access and unauthorized party appears to control the account.","platform":"Instagram","description":"On 5 February 2026, the user was unable to log in to their Instagram account @urban.vibes_07. When attempting to reset the password, they discovered that the registered email address and mobile number had been changed without their consent. Shortly afterward, friends reported receiving suspicious messages from the compromised account asking for money, sharing unknown links, and sending inappropriate content that the user did not create or authorize.","incidentType":"Social media account compromise","accountHandle":"@urban.vibes_07","probableCause":"Unauthorized access to the Instagram account leading to change of recovery credentials and misuse of the account for scams and inappropriate messaging.","impactedParties":["Account owner of @urban.vibes_07","Friends and contacts receiving messages from @urban.vibes_07"],"firstNoticedDate":"2026-02-05","maliciousActivity":{"recipients":"User's friends and contacts on Instagram","impersonation":true,"suspiciousLinksSent":true,"inappropriateContentSent":true,"fraudulentRequestsForMoney":true},"unauthorizedChanges":{"emailChanged":true,"phoneChanged":true,"passwordControlLost":true}},"status":"draft","createdAt":"2026-01-27T05:24:36.323Z"},{"id":5,"userId":"53748919","title":"Instagram account misuse","rawDescription":"On 5 February 2026, I was unable to log in to my Instagram account named @urban.vibes_07. When I attempted to reset my password, I discovered that the registered email ID and mobile number associated with the account had been changed without my consent.\n\nSoon after, my friends informed me that they were receiving suspicious messages from my Instagram account @urban.vibes_07, requesting money and sharing unknown links. Some messages also contained inappropriate content which I never posted.","incidentType":"Social Media Account Compromise","structuredReport":{"impact":{"reputationalRisk":true,"lossOfAccountAccess":true,"potentialFinancialFraud":true,"potentialMalwareOrPhishingSpread":true},"status":"Ongoing – account owner currently does not have access and unauthorized activity is being reported by contacts.","platform":"Instagram","description":"On 5 February 2026, the Instagram account @urban.vibes_07 was compromised. The account owner was unable to log in, and during password recovery attempts discovered that the registered email address and mobile number had been changed without consent. Shortly afterward, friends reported receiving suspicious direct messages from @urban.vibes_07 requesting money, sharing unknown links, and containing inappropriate content that the account owner did not send or authorize.","incidentDate":"2026-02-05","incidentType":"Social Media Account Compromise","accountHandle":"@urban.vibes_07","primaryVictim":{"role":"Account owner","userIdentifier":"@urban.vibes_07"},"suspectedCause":"Account credentials or recovery information were compromised, allowing an attacker to take control and modify the registered email and mobile number.","detectionMethod":"User noticed inability to log in and friends reported suspicious messages from the account","secondaryVictims":["Friends and contacts who received suspicious messages from the compromised account"],"maliciousActivity":{"recipients":"User’s friends and contacts on Instagram","typesOfMessages":["Requests for money","Unknown/possibly malicious links","Inappropriate content"],"messagesSentFromAccount":true},"recommendedActions":["Immediately report the account as hacked via Instagram’s Help Center and in-app reporting tools.","Attempt account recovery using Instagram’s ‘My account was hacked’ process, including identity verification if required.","Inform friends and contacts not to respond to messages from the compromised account, not to send money, and not to click on any links received.","Check associated email accounts and phone numbers for signs of compromise and secure them with strong, unique passwords and multi-factor authentication.","Monitor for any further suspicious activity or impersonation on other platforms linked to the compromised account."],"unauthorizedChanges":{"emailChanged":true,"phoneNumberChanged":true,"passwordCompromised":"Suspected — login blocked and recovery details altered"}},"status":"draft","createdAt":"2026-01-27T05:24:33.767Z"},{"id":4,"userId":"53748919","title":"data robbery","rawDescription":"Myself akshaya ,akshaya@gmail.com, 20years , On 12 January 2026, at 9.20am I received a phone call from an unknown number claiming to be from my bank’s customer care department. The caller said that my bank account would be blocked due to suspicious activity and asked me to verify my details immediately.Trusting the caller, I shared the OTP.\nWithin a few minutes, I received messages showing that ₹48,000 had been debited from my bank account through multiple online transactions. When I checked my bank app, the money was already transferred to unknown accounts.\n","incidentType":"OTP-based Banking Fraud (Vishing/Impersonation of Bank Official)","structuredReport":{"impact":{"description":"Unauthorized debits totaling ₹48,000 from the complainant’s bank account through multiple online transactions to unknown beneficiary accounts.","otherImpact":"Emotional distress and potential risk of further misuse of banking details.","dataCompromise":"Disclosure of OTP linked to the complainant’s bank account authentication.","financialLossINR":48000},"nextSteps":["Immediately contact your bank’s official customer care number (from the back of your card or bank website) and report the fraudulent transactions.","Request the bank to block your debit/credit card, net banking, and any other linked payment services immediately.","Ask the bank to raise a dispute/chargeback for all unauthorized transactions and obtain a written complaint/reference number.","Change your net banking and mobile banking passwords and PINs, and de-register all devices linked to your bank account.","Report the incident on the national cybercrime portal (https://www.cybercrime.gov.in) or the relevant national cyber helpline, providing all details and screenshots.","File a written complaint with the nearest police station or cyber crime cell, attaching bank SMS alerts, transaction statements, and call logs showing the fraud call.","Preserve all evidence, including SMS/WhatsApp messages, call logs, bank notifications, and screenshots of your bank statement, and do not delete any related data from your phone or email.","Monitor your bank accounts and SMS/email alerts regularly for any further suspicious activity and immediately report any new unauthorized transactions.","Do not share OTPs, PINs, CVV, or passwords over phone, SMS, email, or chat in the future, even if the caller claims to be from the bank or a government authority."],"description":"On 12 January 2026 at approximately 9:20 AM, the complainant, Ms. Akshaya, received a phone call from an unknown number. The caller falsely claimed to be from the customer care department of her bank and stated that her bank account would be blocked due to suspicious activity. Under this false pretext, the caller induced her to share a One-Time Password (OTP) purportedly for verification purposes. Shortly after sharing the OTP, multiple unauthorized online transactions took place from her bank account, resulting in a total debit of ₹48,000, which was transferred to unknown accounts without her consent or authorization.","incidentType":"OTP-based Banking Fraud (Vishing/Impersonation of Bank Official)","modeOfAttack":"Phone call (vishing) with fake bank customer care impersonation and fraudulent request for OTP","suggestedCategory":"Online Financial Fraud / Banking Fraud via Impersonation and OTP Deception","generatedReportText":"Cybercrime Report Template\nTo: The Officer-in-Charge, Cyber Cell / [Local Police Station Name]\nSubject: Complaint regarding OTP-based Online Banking Fraud\nComplainant Details: Ms. Akshaya, 20 years, [Address], and [Contact Number].\nIncident Summary: On 12 January 2026, I received a fraudulent phone call from an unknown person impersonating a bank customer care representative, who induced me to share a One-Time Password (OTP), following which unauthorized online transactions totaling ₹48,000 were carried out from my bank account to unknown accounts.\nDate and Time: 12 January 2026, approximately 9:20 AM\nPlatform: Mobile phone call and online banking platform linked to my bank account\nSuspect Details: Unknown caller using an unidentified mobile number, claiming to be from my bank’s customer care department\nChronological Description: On 12 January 2026 at around 9:20 AM, I received a phone call from an unknown mobile number. The caller introduced himself/herself as a representative from my bank’s customer care department and informed me that my bank account was allegedly under threat of being blocked due to suspicious activity. The caller stated that, to prevent the blocking of my account and to verify my identity, I needed to share the One-Time Password (OTP) that I would receive on my registered mobile number. Believing the caller to be a genuine bank representative and concerned about my account being blocked, I shared the OTP that I received. Within a few minutes of sharing the OTP, I started receiving SMS alerts from my bank indicating that multiple online transactions had been carried out from my account. When I checked my bank’s mobile application, I found that a total sum of ₹48,000 had been debited through multiple unauthorized online transactions and transferred to unknown beneficiary accounts without my knowledge or consent. I did not authorize these transactions at any point, and I have been defrauded by the caller who misrepresented themselves as a bank official.\nLoss/Impact: Financial loss of approximately ₹48,000 due to multiple unauthorized online debits from my bank account to unknown accounts, along with mental stress and fear of further misuse of my banking information.\nEvidence List: Screenshots of SMS alerts showing debits of ₹48,000; screenshots/printouts of my bank statement reflecting the unauthorized transactions; details of the incoming fraudulent phone call, including date, time, and caller number (if available); and any other relevant communication records.\nPrayer/Request: I request you to register this complaint and take necessary action under the relevant sections of the IT Act and IPC to recover my funds/data and apprehend the culprit."},"status":"draft","createdAt":"2026-01-27T05:19:34.233Z"},{"id":3,"userId":"53748919","title":"fake email","rawDescription":"suspicious mail from the colleague of our department asking about my credentials  and there is a link after i clicked that my data got stolen and now they were demanding money to unlock a file","incidentType":"Phishing and Ransomware/Data Extortion","structuredReport":{"impact":"Unauthorized access to personal/official data, possible theft or compromise of credentials, and extortion demand for money to unlock encrypted/locked file(s). The exact financial loss is not yet quantified.","nextSteps":["Immediately disconnect the affected device from the internet and any office or home network to prevent further spread of malware.","Do not pay any ransom or transfer any money to the attacker.","Inform your organization’s IT/security team and line manager immediately so they can initiate incident response and secure corporate systems.","Change all passwords for email, system login, banking, and other critical accounts from a clean, uncompromised device.","Enable two-factor authentication (2FA) on important accounts such as email, banking, and work accounts.","Run a full antivirus/anti-malware scan on the affected device and consult IT professionals for system cleanup and forensic analysis.","Preserve all evidence, including the suspicious email, its headers, the malicious link, ransom messages, and any screenshots of the locked files or demands.","File a formal complaint with the local cyber crime police station/cyber cell and/or report the incident on the national cybercrime reporting portal, attaching all evidence.","Monitor bank accounts, email accounts, and other services for any unauthorized access or suspicious activity.","Inform the colleague whose name was used in the email and ask them to verify whether their own account or identity has been compromised."],"description":"The complainant received a suspicious email appearing to be from a colleague in the same department, requesting login credentials and containing a hyperlink. After clicking the link, the complainant’s data appears to have been accessed/compromised and certain files were locked/encrypted. Subsequently, the complainant received a demand for money in exchange for unlocking the affected file(s), indicating an act of data theft and extortion.","incidentType":"Phishing and Ransomware/Data Extortion","modeOfAttack":"Phishing email containing a malicious link","suggestedCategory":"Cyber Fraud, Phishing, Data Theft, and Extortion (Ransomware-like Incident)","generatedReportText":"Cybercrime Report Template\nTo: The Officer-in-Charge, Cyber Cell / [Local Police Station Name]\nSubject: Complaint regarding Phishing, Data Theft, and Cyber Extortion\nComplainant Details: [Full Name], [Age], [Address], and [Contact Number].\nIncident Summary: I received a suspicious email that appeared to be from a colleague in my department, asking for my credentials and containing a link. After clicking the link, my data appears to have been accessed/compromised, and certain files were locked, followed by a demand for money to unlock the affected file(s).\nDate and Time: [Date and Time]\nPlatform: Email (office/personal email account)\nSuspect Details: Email claiming to be from a departmental colleague (exact email address and identity to be verified; currently unknown whether the colleague’s account was compromised), otherwise \"Unknown\".\nChronological Description: On the stated date and time, I received an email that appeared to originate from a colleague within my department. The email requested my credentials and contained a hyperlink. Believing it to be legitimate, I clicked on the link. After doing so, I observed that my data and/or files on the system were affected, with certain files becoming locked or inaccessible. Shortly thereafter, I received a message/demand stating that I must pay money in order to unlock or regain access to the affected file(s). This indicates that my data has been unlawfully accessed/compromised and that I am being subjected to cyber extortion.\nLoss/Impact: Unauthorized access/compromise of my data and possible theft of my login credentials, along with locking/encryption of certain files and an extortion demand for money to restore access. The exact quantum of financial loss is yet to be determined.\nEvidence List: Copy of the suspicious email, email headers, the malicious link/URL, screenshots of the ransom demand, screenshots of locked/encrypted files, and any relevant system logs or correspondence.\nPrayer/Request: I request you to register this complaint and take necessary action under the relevant sections of the IT Act and IPC to recover my funds/data and apprehend the culprit."},"status":"draft","createdAt":"2026-01-27T05:08:43.679Z"},{"id":2,"userId":"53748919","title":"suspicious mail","rawDescription":"suspicious mail from the hr of our department asking about my credentials  and there is a link after i clicked that my money got deducted","incidentType":"Phishing / Credential Harvesting","structuredReport":{"impact":["Unauthorized deduction of money / financial loss","Compromise of login credentials","Potential compromise of personal and/or corporate accounts","Potential broader account takeover or identity theft risk"],"nextSteps":["Immediately contact your bank or card issuer to report unauthorized transactions, block the card or account, and attempt to reverse the charges.","Change passwords for any accounts whose credentials were entered after clicking the link, starting with email, banking, and work-related accounts. Enable multi‑factor authentication where possible.","Report the phishing email to your organization’s IT/security team and follow their incident response procedures. Provide the email, headers, and link if available.","Run a reputable antivirus/malware scan on the device used to click the link to detect any malware.","Monitor bank, credit card, and important online accounts for further suspicious activity and set up alerts where possible.","If significant personal data was exposed, consider placing a fraud alert or credit freeze with relevant credit bureaus, as applicable in your country."],"description":"The user received an email appearing to be from their department HR asking for credentials and containing a link. After clicking the link, unauthorized financial transactions occurred, indicating likely credential theft and fraud.","incidentType":"Phishing / Credential Harvesting","modeOfAttack":"Email phishing with malicious link leading to credential theft and subsequent unauthorized financial transactions","suggestedCategory":"Security Incident / Phishing and Fraud"},"status":"draft","createdAt":"2026-01-27T05:01:54.701Z"},{"id":1,"userId":"53748919","title":"suspicious mail","rawDescription":"suspicious mail from the hr of our department asking about my credentials  and there is a link after i clicked that my money got deducted","incidentType":"Phishing / Credential Harvesting","structuredReport":{"impact":"Compromised credentials, unauthorized financial loss, and potential ongoing access to personal or work accounts by the attacker","nextSteps":["Immediately contact your bank or payment provider to report unauthorized transactions and request card/account blocking and chargeback where possible.","Change passwords immediately for any accounts that may have been entered after clicking the link (email, HR/employee portal, banking, etc.), and enable multi-factor authentication where available.","Report the incident to your organization’s IT/security team, providing the suspicious email, link, and time of access so they can investigate and block similar emails.","Scan your device with up-to-date antivirus/anti-malware tools; if available, involve IT to check for any installed malware or remote access tools.","Monitor bank statements and relevant accounts closely for additional suspicious activity and set up alerts for new transactions or logins.","If significant financial loss or identity theft is suspected, file a report with local law enforcement and, where applicable, relevant cybercrime/consumer protection authorities."],"description":"The user received an email appearing to be from their department HR requesting credentials and containing a link. After clicking the link and likely submitting information or enabling a transaction, money was deducted from their account, indicating a successful phishing and possible financial fraud.","incidentType":"Phishing / Credential Harvesting","modeOfAttack":"Email phishing with malicious link leading to credential theft and unauthorized financial transaction","suggestedCategory":"Security Incident > Phishing > Financial Fraud / Account Compromise"},"status":"draft","createdAt":"2026-01-27T05:01:51.776Z"}]
