2:54:39 AM [express] POST /api/reports/generate 200 in 19161ms :: {"incidentType":"phishing","structuredReport":{"incidentType":"PHISHING","description":"To,\nThe Officer-in-Charge,\nCyber Crime Police Station.\n\nSubject: Complaint regarding phishing and unauthorised online banking transaction.\n\nI, Priya, wish to report a fraudulent incident involving an online phishing attempt that resulted in unauthorised transfer of funds from my bank account.\n\n1. Incident Details:\n   - Date & Time of Incident: Information not available at the time of reporting\n   - Mode of Communication: Electronic message containing a malicious link (likely SMS or instant message)\n   - Suspect Details: The individuals or entities behind the fraudulent message and the beneficiary of the transferred funds are unknown at this stage.\n\n2. Chronological Description of the Incident:\n   I received a message stating that my bank account would be blocked and instructing me to click a provided link to verify my account immediately. Believing the message to be genuine, I clicked on the link. The link led to a fraudulent webpage resembling a banking portal, where I entered my internet banking username, password, and a One-Time Password (OTP) that I received. Shortly after providing these details, an unauthorised transaction was initiated from my bank account without my consent. Within minutes, a sum of ₹45,000 was transferred from my account to an unknown account. I then received transaction alert messages from my bank, after which I realised that I had been defrauded through a phishing link.\n\n3. Financial Loss Details:\n   An amount of ₹45,000 (Rupees Forty-Five Thousand only) has been debited from my bank account and transferred to an unknown account without my authorisation.\n\n4. Evidence List:\n   - Screenshot or copy of the fraudulent message that stated “Your bank account will be blocked. Click here to verify immediately.”\n   - Details and URL of the phishing website that opened after clicking the link, if retrievable.\n   - Bank transaction alert messages showing the debit of ₹45,000 and the time of transaction.\n   - Bank statement or mini-statement showing the unauthorised transaction.\n   - Any email/SMS alerts received from the bank related to login or OTP usage.\n\n5. Request for Action:\n   I respectfully request the Cyber Crime Police Station to:\n   - Register this complaint under relevant sections of law pertaining to cyber fraud, phishing, and unauthorised online banking transactions.\n   - Coordinate with the concerned bank and payment service providers to trace and freeze the beneficiary account(s) where ₹45,000 has been transferred, subject to feasibility.\n   - Initiate an investigation to identify the perpetrators who sent the fraudulent message and operated the phishing website.\n   - Assist in recovery of the lost amount to the extent possible and provide necessary guidance for securing my bank accounts and digital credentials.\n   - Issue any appropriate advisories or directions to prevent further misuse of my personal and banking information.\n\nI am ready to provide any further information, documents, or statements required during the course of the investigation.\n\nYours faithfully,\nPriya","modeOfAttack":"Electronic message containing a phishing link","impact":"Unauthorised transfer of ₹45,000 from the complainant's bank account to an unknown account.","suggestedCategory":"Online banking fraud / digital payment phishing","extractedDetails":{"complainant_name":"Priya","loss_amount":"45000","currency":"INR","message_content":"Your bank account will be blocked. Click here to verify immediately.","credentials_entered":"banking username, password, and OTP","transaction_status":"₹45,000 transferred to an unknown account","alert_received":"transaction alert messages","timeframe":"Within minutes after entering credentials"},"nextSteps":["Immediately contact your bank's customer care or fraud helpline, report the unauthorised transaction, and request to block your internet banking, debit/credit cards, and any further transactions from your account.","Submit a written complaint to your bank branch detailing the phishing message, time of incident, and the unauthorised debit of ₹45,000, and request reversal/freeze of funds if still possible.","Capture and securely store screenshots of the fraudulent message, the phishing website (if still accessible), and the transaction alerts you received, as these will be crucial evidence.","File an online cyber crime complaint at the official national cyber crime reporting portal applicable in your jurisdiction, attaching all available evidence and bank statements.","Visit the nearest Cyber Crime Police Station or local police station to formally file an FIR, carrying your ID proof, bank statements, transaction SMS, and a printed copy of your complaint.","Change all your banking-related passwords and PINs immediately, and ensure that the OTP or any other sensitive information is never shared or entered on links received via unsolicited messages.","Enable additional security measures with your bank, such as transaction limits, email/SMS alerts for all debits, and, if available, app-based authenticators instead of SMS-based OTP alone.","Monitor your bank accounts and other financial/online accounts closely over the next few weeks for any further suspicious activity and report immediately if anything unusual occurs."],"guidance":{"immediate":["Disconnect your device from the internet to stop further data transmission.","Close all browser tabs and do not interact with the suspicious link or sender.","If you provided bank details, call your bank immediately to freeze your accounts."],"security":["Change passwords for your email and any affected online accounts immediately.","Enable Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) on all sensitive accounts.","Run a full antivirus scan on your device to check for installed malware."],"evidence":["Take screenshots of the phishing email or SMS, including the sender's details.","Do not delete the original message; it contains technical headers needed for investigation.","Note down the URL of the malicious website if you clicked a link."],"nextSteps":["Report the incident to the official National Cyber Crime Reporting Portal (cybercrime.gov.in).","Notify the organization being impersonated (e.g., your bank or service provider).","Monitor your financial statements for any unauthorized transactions for the next 30 days."]}}}












































